self-paced lab where we'll

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.590
create and connect to a
Cloud SQL MySQL instance

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.630
and perform some
basic SQL operations.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.889
So stick around for that.

00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:36.930
KELLY GROVER: If you're
using a Postgres database

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.191
engine, no problem.

00:00:38.191 --> 00:00:39.690
We'll point you to
that lab as well.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.020
ANKUSH AGARWAL: Cloud SQL is a
fully managed database service

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.040
that lets you hand off to
Google the often time-consuming

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.670
yet necessary tasks.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.790
Think of applying patches and
updates or managing backups

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.560
and configuring replications.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.010
This allows you to focus
on building great apps.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.500
KELLY GROVER: Whether you're
using MySQL or Postgres,

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.590
Cloud SQL allows you to set
up and configure an instance

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.300
in just a few steps.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.440
For better performance,
you can keep your data

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.110
close to the
services that need it

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:15.380
by selecting the most suitable
geographical region to run

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.190
your resources.

00:01:20.786 --> 00:01:22.160
ANKUSH AGARWAL:
This hands-on lab

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.950
